{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do","id":1140399,"title":"What can an unarmed technocrat do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-14T19:32:42-07:00","id":1140399,"title":"What can an unarmed technocrat do?","content":"For Mages of all kinds being prepared is essential to surviving a battle. A mage needs their wand, plasma caster, eldritch skull, super car, etc... to do magic. I was wondering what a Technocrat can do when they are <i>completely</i> unarmed and unequipped. I always hear about genetic, psychic, or cybernetic modifications on technocrats, but if a technocrat is caught bare and doesn't have any what can he do? Are there non physical foci that can be used by technocrats, or is he completely out of options? <br /> <br /> Any thoughts are appreciated<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16848-brassfist","name":"Brassfist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T20:29:08-07:00","id":1140412,"title":"","content":"Martial Arts, for one. Putting aside the mystical themes - which obviously don't come into play with the strictly rationalist Technocracy - an Enlightened agent can work wonders with the proper application of physical might and scientific principles.<br /> <br /> Speaking of scientific principles, a Technocract could employ them in conjunction with materials lying around to do their work. Basically imagine MacGuyver, except with Enlightened levels of brilliance.<br /> <br /> Even &quot;technobabble&quot; can be used in creative ways. Like a Technocrat forcing a person to puke, just by rattling off the chemicals contained in processed foods. Or altering the person's behavior by citing obscure psychology studies, so the target thinks that acting in a certain way is normal or even expected. Or causing a machine to break down by talking about its many technical limitations, followed by a well-placed slap to the side. Some of this technobabble involves providing information that directly influences people, while others are simply the Technocrat proving their authority on the subject at hand, and &quot;letting nature take its course&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T20:29:47-07:00","id":1140413,"title":"","content":"Meditation, Observation, &quot;Doing the math&quot; Psychology, etc... it REALLY depends on what their spheres are and some spheres work better with particular instraments than others in the Technocratic paradigm. Bare in mind what &quot;looks&quot; like a Technocratic instrament might not be the case. If say &quot;Doing the math&quot; is their focii and they might regularly use computers or a sliderule but when push comes to shove they can do the math in their head its just not going to be as impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T21:04:58-07:00","id":1140421,"title":"","content":"These are great examples! For an enforcer type character I always see 'Hotshotting' (damage amp for gun) as an example. In the technocratic book it was listed as being effected by the Hollywood influence that guns shot by professionals would do more damage. How would I express this as a focus? Is there a name for meme as foci? or is it just that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16848-brassfist","name":"Brassfist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T23:09:30-07:00","id":1140432,"title":"","content":"As listed already, Especially the latest books list a lot of Magick and tools that are simply psychology and 'rational mind' based.<br /> <br /> Psychology and Social Dominion - This is a big one. Body language, observation, conversational tricks, the way you dress and act..all those things can be used especially for Mind procedures. Even a stern look directly into anothers' eyes can become a tool for influence, and a charmling smile which can attract, positively influence and make others have decisions in your favor more effectively than any unenlightened person could pull off. The MiBs and people of the Syndicate are pros at this.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts - As was mentioned, the Technocracy *does* put training and value in this, based on enlightened studies and principles, They don't do call the moves fancy esoteric names, and it's not Do per se, but they have enough examples of Agents dropping the hammer down in form of even aggravated damage, enlightened dodging and enhanced mind-based coordination.<br /> Read the HDYDT intro story for an example of John Courage just...obliterating a guy with this.<br /> <br /> The above mentioned 'MacGuyvering' - Finnicky, but it works. The Technocrats *are* enlightened, and based on their principles, they can come up with MacGyveresque applications of mundane tools in a pinch. It's not as crazy as probably a Son Of Ether would be able to employ some things that fall under their expertise, but enlightened physics, extraordinary applications of materials, combined with their hypermathematics can do, no pun intended, wonders.<br /> <br /> Enlightened observation - Mostly limited to level 1 spheres, but even when not aided with, ahem, stimulants, the enlightened that are trained in hypermathematics, observational techniques, scientific principles and logic can do a lot of Sphere 1 feats based on their 'rational understanding' alone. It's certainly nothing that blows them to absolute supernatural levels, but subtle enhancements of the mental stats, having insight into the process and conclusion of complex events and the like certainly would work without any additional aids. In their head they are simply utterly focusing on what's happening, with mathemetic formulae and textbook teachings rattling down. It's almost a form of Technocratic meditation.<br /> <br /> Meditation - Speaking of..they do this. Meditation, focusing techniques, even stuff like Yoga is actually in the Technocratic repertoire. Minus the fancy archaic superstitions - it's all SCIENCE and rational logic behind ordering the mind, controlling your body.<br /> <br /> Hidden Features - The Syndicate is big on this. There are a lot of, ahem, 'Hidden Features' built into normal consumer products out there that pass through Technocracy-owned or -sponsored production lines. Wether the product *actually* had special things installed, or the operative simply believes it does is kind of up for debate, isn:t it..?<br /> <br /> Coincidence! - Likewise, this. This is the weirdest thing they can sometimes pull off. I forget which book had an example for this, but basically a MiB operative scans a ceiling, and just happens to *notice* that it is about to crumble down on an enemy. They jump back just in time, while the other gets crushed. The operative themselves does not even think that magick happened - but it was them that subconciously caused the actual structural failure with a forces procedure. This is probably the most..esoteric and grey example of Technocratic magick, as the one causing it is not even aware. Even in *their* mind it was a pure coincidence. It's like an absolute wildcard in a normally very structured and predictable approach to things.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> And yeah, Brassfist - the Technocracy can work with modern technological and Hollywood-ish memes. Although in *their* mind there must be a logical reason for it to work. Enhanced Technocratic training in martial arts mentioned above, but also rigorous application of enlightened principles to firearms combat can do a lot. Psychology combined with subtle adjustments of the firearm is what makes the 'Hotshotting' rote work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":".  Typo fixings! 09-15-2017, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T10:18:06-07:00","id":1140540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1140432#post1140432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meditation - Speaking of..they do this. Meditation, focusing techniques, even stuff like Yoga is actually in the Technocratic repertoire. Minus the fancy archaic superstitions - it's all SCIENCE and rational logic behind ordering the mind, controlling your body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Biofeedback can justify a fair amount of things. Even more so if you're one of those Progenitor eugenic ubermench types.<br /> <br /> Excellent post, BTW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T12:36:49-07:00","id":1141848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1140540#post1140540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Biofeedback can justify a fair amount of things. Even more so if you're one of those Progenitor eugenic ubermench types.<br /> <br /> Excellent post, BTW.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What Exactly is Bio Feedback? And what would you use it as within the paradigm of a Progenitor? I have never seen the term, but I imagine it is for life effects correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16848-brassfist","name":"Brassfist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T15:47:31-07:00","id":1141921,"title":"","content":"I'm nt sold on Technocrats MacGuyvering to a great extent. The BIG flaw in the Technocratic Paradigm is the reliance on very specific Tools to do the job. Iirc in revised (cannt speak for 20th) but while a Mage of the Traditions can pull off an Effect with very little, a TechnoMage requires some Tools and a bit of inspiration and a Technocrat needs their tried and tested gadgetry and formulae. This is in fact WHY the Virtual Adepts and Sons of Ether ended up leaving the Union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T16:25:12-07:00","id":1141931,"title":"","content":"<b> Revised Syndicate Convention Book </b> mentions \u201cExpertise\u201d as a possible focus: in M20 terms, you can use a 4+-dot Ability as an Instrument. This is usually done for Coincidental Effects, but can be done for Vulgar ones as well: snatching bullets out of midair as per Ozymandius from <i>Watchmen</i>, running along walls or through the trees as in <i>Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon</i>, and similar feats can be attempted by Syndics on the basis of \u201cI'm just that good\u201d. I'd also allow NWO agent access to this sort of thing. Meanwhile, ItXers, Progenitors, and Space Marines tend to be more gear-reliant, and more likely to McGuyver solutions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T17:03:08-07:00","id":1141939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brassfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1141848#post1141848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What Exactly is Bio Feedback? And what would you use it as within the paradigm of a Progenitor? I have never seen the term, but I imagine it is for life effects correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically using various instruments to keep track of your body's functions - heart rate, respiration, body temp, brainwaves, etc. - so that you can moderate them to some degree, and in theory eventually control the physical processes such as heart rate, muscle tone, skin conductivity, pain perception, and so on. It's more or less a scientific effort at the sort of feats traditionally attributes to Eastern mystics. <br /> <br /> For the Progenitors (and all Conventions, really), it would basically be a process of using various monitors (eventually getting down to just a smart watch type device or even a cybernetic implant that mimics Life 1 and Mind 1) to train one's body to perform certain functions and effects at will (as a set of Rotes, mostly involving Life 2). Things like boosting adrenaline output, increasing blood clotting of wounds, getting the equivalent of a full night's sleep with only an hour's worth of meditation, faking your own death, and the like.<br /> <br /> It's also really suitable for Etherites and Virtual Adepts, as well as more technology minded Akashics, Verbena, Hollowers, Ecstatics, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:51:43-07:00","id":1141986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1141921#post1141921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm nt sold on Technocrats MacGuyvering to a great extent. The BIG flaw in the Technocratic Paradigm is the reliance on very specific Tools to do the job. Iirc in revised (cannt speak for 20th) but while a Mage of the Traditions can pull off an Effect with very little, a TechnoMage requires some Tools and a bit of inspiration and a Technocrat needs their tried and tested gadgetry and formulae. This is in fact WHY the Virtual Adepts and Sons of Ether ended up leaving the Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>The opposite actually. The Technocratic Paradigm is generally MORE convenient than a comparative effect done traditionally. What happens is they get BONUS's for using specific technogadgets.<br /> <br /> The Virtual Adepts and the Sons of Ether left the union because both couldn't handle the idea of the world the Union was building. Both have paradigms that allow the infinite and the impossible. The unexpected to happen.<br /> <br /> The Union isn't said to be calcifying reality for nothing. They want to take the subjective reality, where magic is real and the rules are flexible, and craft rock solid, set in stone rules for how reality works. Thereby undoing magic. The VA and SoE like reality being flexible, and so left. OR at least in the SoE's case, their part of the set in stone reality got written out. So they took their ball and went home.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Mage of the traditions requires incantations, odd actions, etc. To invoke an effect. Technocrats can oftentimes just DO their effects. &quot;I angle my polarized mirror shades the way they taught me in training so that I can see ghosts.&quot; &quot;I load the gun and chamber a round. Chk. Chk.&quot; &quot;I talk to him and implant a suggestion.&quot; &quot;I get the crowd riled up with a Propaganda laden speech.&quot; &quot;I punch the guy in the kidney REALLY HARD.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T06:52:35-07:00","id":1142122,"title":"","content":"What I mean Enginseer is that the Technocratic Paradigm is less flexible (as the rules themselves said, a Mage can try and make something happen by a force of will, a TechnoMage can add some blagging to pull off an effect but a Technocrat Needs his Foci). For example the Mirrorshades trick only works with the special issue Mirrorshades, regular ray-bans just don't cut it because there is a special material in the lenses on the Agent issued ones. They don't teach Agents how to use a gun better they issue them with specialist firearms that employs State of the Art technology and requires specialist training to use. <br /> <br /> On the flip side there are a whole bunch of things that DO work. One of the most dangerous technocrats my players met in he campaign session was the Syndicate Senior Analyst they encountered during a raid. His technocratic paradigm was based around Statistical prediction, Probability Frames, Non-Vocal communication profiling and a few other things. He also had some field-work combat training. No toys apart from having watched a security video feed of the cabal in action. He took the Akashic apart in close combat, Forces, Mind, Entropy and Time. <br /> <br /> Another Campaign totally freaked one of the Cabal as he got interviewed casually in the street by a MiB. No gadgets, no phone, no cyberware that could be seen (Mage was a VA and had checked) he even took of his Mirrorshades. The VA only realised something as up when he started volunteering information that he wouldn't normally share with anyone BUT the Cabal and describing event in detail that he couldn't previously recall that clearly. Communication and memory regression themed Procedures and Techniques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T07:25:13-07:00","id":1142136,"title":"","content":"No, special issue mirrorshades give you a bonus -1 to diff. Same for the rest. The gadgets aren't the tech stuff paradigm, and it's gadgets do stuff that forms the technomancers paradigm.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic paradigm is defined by rules, laws of physics, chemistry, biology, psychology and statistics. How to apply these laws in a practical manner is what most Technocrats on the front lines learn. They don't go into the lab to learn how to build a fancy gun. They learn how to set standard explosives in the expert manner required to shape the explosion for maximum effect.<br /> <br /> Technomancers use gadgets. Technocrats use science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T07:37:28-07:00","id":1142143,"title":"","content":"I'm with Enginseer mostly, except that Technomancers can also use science instead of gadgets, if it's from non-widely accepted theories, fringe stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T08:03:36-07:00","id":1142155,"title":"","content":"Idem, I think the same. Neither use gadgets until they use them. NWO uses &quot;special training&quot; to do all kind mind tricks with their attire, and they also use gadgets (Q Division). However, this isn't something that sets Technocrats appart, Etherites often use &quot;advanced mathematics&quot;, martial arts (for their fistcuff fans and secret agents), and perform extraordinary feats using science in an Awakened way (point in case, I'm currently playing a detective Etherite that can uses his deductive skills as a Focus for various sensory effects).<br /> <br /> If a technomancer ( has to use a &quot;special&quot; item to do an effect or just a normal item used trough &quot;special training&quot; (such is the case with NWO mirrorshaeds to protect against mind control) depends on certain elements of the Paradigm. While all Technocrats could theoretically learn to use mirrorshades to do Mind tricks, most don't, the mirrorshade thing it's a common NWO Focus, but not so common among other Conventions. For instance, I don't imagine Iteration X using mirrorshades as a focus (at least not commonly), they probably would use some kind of scifi stuff (like a helmet that blocks deviant psionics, or injected nanobots that do the same). Albeit all Technocrats could theoretically learn how to use a regular gun to do amazing (and impossible) stuff, this requires &quot;special training&quot; that not ALL technocrats have. In this case, the &quot;special training&quot; it's the &quot;gadget&quot;, you can chose it among your Foci (guns). In M20 lore this would be called a <i>Practice</i>...your Paradigm it's what you believe, your Practice it's how you have learned to do it.<br /> <br /> A NWO agent can use mirrorshades to do some Mind tricks, but to hack a computer he can't use mirrorshades (unless they're special gadgets). An Etherite may be able to kick some serious ass with their martial arts learned in the Tibet, but probably needs a some form of tech to hack a computer (albeit with Etherites one never knows)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T08:36:01-07:00","id":1142166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1140412#post1140412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial Arts, for one. Putting aside the mystical themes - which obviously don't come into play with the strictly rationalist Technocracy - an Enlightened agent can work wonders with the proper application of physical might and scientific principles.<br /> <br /> Speaking of scientific principles, a Technocract could employ them in conjunction with materials lying around to do their work. Basically imagine MacGuyver, except with Enlightened levels of brilliance.<br /> <br /> Even &quot;technobabble&quot; can be used in creative ways. Like a Technocrat forcing a person to puke, just by rattling off the chemicals contained in processed foods. Or altering the person's behavior by citing obscure psychology studies, so the target thinks that acting in a certain way is normal or even expected. Or causing a machine to break down by talking about its many technical limitations, followed by a well-placed slap to the side. Some of this technobabble involves providing information that directly influences people, while others are simply the Technocrat proving their authority on the subject at hand, and &quot;letting nature take its course&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first two would potentially work depending on the circumstances, but I'm not actually sold on the last one. The problem with it is that there's no direct line between speaking technobabble and creating the intended effect other than, basically, magic words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T08:58:10-07:00","id":1142173,"title":"","content":"Except that's actually a Canon procedure. It's in the guide to the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T09:32:54-07:00","id":1142186,"title":"","content":"A lot of maintaining Paradigm is going to be ST call. I know people want hard and fast rules but its probably going to be more about what feels right. An Etherite might Macguyer up a death ray, a Technocrat would do more down to earth measures. I imagine using Entropy and Mind along with Sensory effects are probably the easiest to justify. A Technocrat isn't going to teleport with just their mind, but biofeed back to heal wounds, or superior knowledge of the body to punch harder either way I imagine its going to be the most especially subtle of things, the most coincidence of coincidences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T10:05:08-07:00","id":1142195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first two would potentially work depending on the circumstances, but I'm not actually sold on the last one. The problem with it is that there's no direct line between speaking technobabble and creating the intended effect other than, basically, magic words.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that's actually a Canon procedure. It's in the guide to the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I imagine the Technocrats doing the procedure won't call it &quot;technobabble&quot;, wishful thinking can't change how a machine opperates! .They obviously are assessing your machine with their enlightened expertice and introducing reasonable doubt about it's quality, their words on the subject make perfect sense (for someone with the knowledge), and if the machine doesn't work it's not their fault.<br /> <br /> That being said, I wouldn't allow this instrument unless you're actually an expert on the matter (I.E, no technobabbling about a biological procedure without Medicine or Biology). Otherwise it's just ludicrous (well, more ludicrous), technocrats would be admiting that science isn't objective because your perception or opinion about the matter change how it works, thats Etherite level weirdness (and beyond).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-20-2017, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T10:48:25-07:00","id":1142217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1142195#post1142195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, I imagine the Technocrats doing the procedure won't call it &quot;technobabble&quot;, wishful thinking can't change how a machine opperates! .They obviously are assessing your machine with their enlightened expertice and introducing reasonable doubt about it's quality, their words on the subject make perfect sense (for someone with the knowledge), and if the machine doesn't work it's not their fault.<br /> <br /> That being said, I wouldn't allow this instrument unless you're actually an expert on the matter (I.E, no technobabbling about a biological procedure without Medicine or Biology). Otherwise it's just ludicrous (well, more ludicrous), technocrats would be admiting that science isn't objective because your perception or opinion about the matter change how it works, thats Etherite level weirdness (and beyond).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the question boils down to what you are doing to make it not work. If you are actually using the spheres in question presumably you have the sciences to back it up(Medicine for life) if you are just using advanced psychological proceedures pure bullshitting might be applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T11:08:32-07:00","id":1142226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1142217#post1142217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think the question boils down to what you are doing to make it not work. If you are actually using the spheres in question presumably you have the sciences to back it up(Medicine for life) if you are just using advanced psychological proceedures pure bullshitting might be applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, even a scientist understands the psychological power of a lie, if it comes from a perceived authority on the subject. Even if the agent cites a study that is bullshit, if they can make their listener believe it, it can change how they think (if only by virtue of the target believing really hard that they ought to be thinking in a certain way).<br /> <br /> Although that sort of thing could extend even to Life effects as well. The Placebo Effect is a known factor in medical science, to the point where it's firmly in the Consensus. If the right words - coming from a supposed expert medical authority - can plant the idea of a medical malady in a person's head, it could trick the body into manifesting the symptoms on its own. Mind over matter isn't just for spiritualists and psychics, but is arguably scientific fact...to a certain degree. A Technocrat won't be able to talk a person into spontaneously growing tentacles, but he could make him run a fever, have a seizure, or begin vomiting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T12:31:52-07:00","id":1142261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1142195#post1142195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, I imagine the Technocrats doing the procedure won't call it &quot;technobabble&quot;, wishful thinking can't change how a machine opperates! .They obviously are assessing your machine with their enlightened expertice and introducing reasonable doubt about it's quality, their words on the subject make perfect sense (for someone with the knowledge), and if the machine doesn't work it's not their fault.<br /> <br /> That being said, I wouldn't allow this instrument unless you're actually an expert on the matter (I.E, no technobabbling about a biological procedure without Medicine or Biology). Otherwise it's just ludicrous (well, more ludicrous), technocrats would be admiting that science isn't objective because your perception or opinion about the matter change how it works, thats Etherite level weirdness (and beyond).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Anthropic Principle is firmly entrenched in the Technocratic Paradigm. They actually acknowledge that YES wishful thinking CAN change how a machine operates. That's why they shoot people who disagree with them. That's why they consider deviancy actually harmful, because your thoughts DO matter. Your thoughts CAN change things.<br /> <br /> Everything they do only makes sense if they're aware of the greater truths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T13:24:52-07:00","id":1142284,"title":"","content":"Being aware of the greater truths, such as they are, still does not mean you can use them. Paradigm is King and while it lets you change the world it also restricts those changes to what you KNOW how to do. The Technocracy know about reality deviants who warp reality and they are dangerous because those warps threaten the Technocratic Paradigm and is grip on reality. The Technocracy have very carefully and precisely constructed their Paradigm around principles that became Science and Technology but they are bound by those principled, yes they can massively reach beyond what the UnEnlightened can do but without the tools and methodologies of those principles they can do no more than a regular person. They exchanged flexibility and randomness for stolid reliability (more often coincidental). Now it can be VERY hard to divest a Technocrat from those tools with some of them being advanced theorems and principles or mental conditioning and others being Cyberware and bioware but they will find it VERY hard to achieve something on the fly, this is why things like Iteration X do not have Trinary Computer Systems (but do have access to AI), the Progenitors use specialist compounds and medical gear but are unlikely to try and use their own blood and a knife, no matter what a MiB agent does he will not be firing plasma bolts at anyone without a plasma gun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T17:43:55-07:00","id":1142359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1142284#post1142284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being aware of the greater truths, such as they are, still does not mean you can use them. Paradigm is King and while it lets you change the world it also restricts those changes to what you KNOW how to do. The Technocracy know about reality deviants who warp reality and they are dangerous because those warps threaten the Technocratic Paradigm and is grip on reality. The Technocracy have very carefully and precisely constructed their Paradigm around principles that became Science and Technology but they are bound by those principled, yes they can massively reach beyond what the UnEnlightened can do but without the tools and methodologies of those principles they can do no more than a regular person. They exchanged flexibility and randomness for stolid reliability (more often coincidental). Now it can be VERY hard to divest a Technocrat from those tools with some of them being advanced theorems and principles or mental conditioning and others being Cyberware( and bioware but they will find it VERY hard to achieve something on the fly, this is why things like Iteration X do not have Trinary Computer Systems (but do have access to AI), the Progenitors use specialist compounds and medical gear but are unlikely to try and use their own blood and a knife, no matter what a MiB agent does he will not be firing plasma bolts at anyone without a plasma gun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradigm is King, and the Technocratic Paradigm is not &quot;The Principles that Became Science and Technology&quot; Science and Technology are a product of the larger Paradigm of Reason. THE End product, the crown jewel so to speak. But not the be all end all of what can be done.<br /> <br /> The cornerstone of the Technocratic Paradigm is the Anthropic Principle. What is believed is reality. This is why the NWO controls what is believed via public education, manipulation of public perception. What the Traditions let each individual mage muddle along towards on their path to personal enlightment, every enlightened agent starts out knowing. This even ties in mechanically with 'psionic paradigms' where the Technocrat can declare certain spheres psionic at chargen. If they so choose. Meaning that 'focusless sphere' thing? Technocrats can potentially start with that. That MiB agent could coalesce plasma in his hands and chuck it like a fastball.<br /> <br /> Now, most don't because working with tools is useful. If you fire a plasma cannon and paradox backlash strikes. If you're quick enough you can drop the cannon and back away because the backlash hits the cannon, not you. If you are the source of the effect... well YOU get hit.<br /> <br /> Working with tools is just generally all around BETTER than directly working magic. So, when at all possible, Technocrats use tools.<br /> <br /> The Paradigm of Reason produced Science and Technology, and shares many traits with it's offspring. But it is a fundamentally different beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T03:37:53-07:00","id":1142450,"title":"","content":"That's dangerously close to the Purple Paradigm and in Revised at least it flat out states &quot;No Foci No Effect&quot; for a Technocratic Mage, i fact its pretty much that most of the time for most Mages but sone can try to just enact a force of will into an Effect. The Technocracy is aware of the Consensus but NOT the Purple Paradigm. The purpose of Paradigm is literally &quot;From the PoV of your Mage these are the hidden laws and secrets to how Reality Works and you can use those Rules to manipulate Reality to you desires&quot; the Union Paradigm is the &quot;One true Paradigm of Enlightened Science&quot; and what Reality Deviants do &quot;damages the fragile structure of Reality by improper use of the rules the Union has learned&quot;. <br /> <br /> An MiB Agent has literally No Way of conjuring plasma between his hands and throwing it. That is what the cybernetic guns are for. Just like if you mute a Hermetic Mage that will massively limit what they can achieve. Higher levels of Ar\u00eate mean you can start circumventing these restrictions in Paradigm but no amount of Enochian chanting is going to let a Verbana summon anything. The Technocratic Union hasn't unlocked some great secret that lets them shift reality to their whim, they are trapped by the Truth they helped create. As soon as you start working around that the entire concept of Paradigm, Avatar(Genius) and Ar\u00eate goes out the window.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T03:42:13-07:00","id":1142452,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that the TU sometimes runs on &quot;Science&quot; that is so far advanced, as to be indistinguishable from magic. In addition to that the Technocracy does some mad prepwork (or at least pretends to do it), allowing Unionists to pull off some spectacular stunts.<br /> <br /> Can a technocraft turn a kitchen knife into a gun using 'magic words'? Of course not. But he can trigger the catchphrase that will trigger the device hidden in its handle (thanks to the Syndicates efforts, alot of mundane household appliances have hidden functions) that collapses the waveform of the knife and then reconfiguring its material form to the agents need with the help of real time sattelite assisted computing.<br /> <br /> Can a technocrat stranded naked in the wilds by a reality deviant wrestle the hungry bear next to him? Well that depends on his combat training. However if the mage has benefited from proper training he can adopt certain mannerisms, which combined with his slightly altered body scent (a standart small scale physiological alteration done to field agents, usually just piggybacked onto a flu shot for convinience sake) will trigger a genetic sequence added to the species in 1907. It was added to a sample specimen and then transmitted to the rest of the species via complex quantum entanglement procedures that searched for DNA of similar configuration. Yes I know that's how sleepers told you is not how quantum entanglement works. Explaining the exact physics behind it would take you years to understand without the use of advanced psychometric learning techniques. Anyway trigger the sequence, the bear turns docile.<br /> <br /> Can a technocrat just simply step through time and space? well space is really relative and certain natural distortions can be abused. That's of course very tricky, by and all space is rather sturdy. But you can allways use the mainframe hub of your area in a bind by uttering a specific sound combined with certain muscle contractions. We have a statistical analytic programm running on the mainframe that'll predict when someone next enacts this trigger, then opens a micro-spatial-fissure, feeding you information from its side via ultrasound directly into your subconcious and reading your responses from pupil dilation. Should have seen those superstitionists when I suddenly vanished and popped back up behind them.<br /> <br /> In the end alot of what is possible or not possible is a question of ST decree, but the Union can justify just about any effect using the vast infrastructure of highly advanced sci fi technology. How far they can take it probably depends on what mood you want to use for them. I know some who think the union (aside from the VEs) should be played as basically a normal government agency whose technology is just about as advanced as modern technology, just with maybe a few years ahead and them being really good at it (mechanically represented through the benefit of spellcasting mechanics). Such an NWO agent can of course only use his Data spehere to spy on people when he has actual drones in the air and teleportation is right out of the window. That is superstitionist talk! On the other hand you can play the union as being centuries ahead of normal humanity due to their enlightened understanding (easily doable using magic) and only slowly introducing the tech to the sleepers at an ever growing pace. Such a Unionist doesn't use a spydrone because he has to or because it's particularily easier. He does so because it gives him plausible deniability. Because he works together with sleeper agents whom he exalts through his exemplary use of modern technology. Not everyone has an education in basic hypertech (yet), so everytime a technocrat is forced to use instruments a sleeper can't understand and that seem miraculous to him, the sleeper misinterprets science as magic and the timetable needs to be adjusted ever so slightly behind. This TU uses bleeding edge science instruments to inspire, not because they have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T04:17:55-07:00","id":1142460,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's some good stuff there, some really good stuff there. <br /> But again this is very much what Rotes/Procedures are for. The big Trap in Mage comes down to I have Spheres X,Y,Z and I want to roll Ar\u00eate and everything else falls to the wayside with every tradition and convention ultimately doing the same things and the Paradigm becoming a flavour text coating. That's why when I have more experienced Mage players when they come up with character Paradigms describe not only their How Do I Dos but also investigate the limits of how that Paradigm can employ their Spheres and what they Can't (currently) do. The Verbana and Ecstatic magi are less likely to be throwing fireballs than the OoH or Akashic Brotherhood, likewise Syndicate Agents probably won't be packing heat (while they may well have Prime and Forces) whereas their Void Engineer and MiB counterparts migh be loaded for Bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T08:35:41-07:00","id":1142534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The cornerstone of the Technocratic Paradigm is the Anthropic Principle. What is believed is reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>No and no.<br /> <br /> A: &quot;What is believed is reality&quot; it's not the Anthropic Principle. The Anthropic Principle it's that the universe it's shaped to hold human life and consciousness, that the universe it's compatible with human existence and things that would not be conducent to human consciousness are pushed to the other side of the Gauntlet (to their own realms made for them). Belief has nothing to do with it, consciousness and biology has a lot to do with it. This principle basically states that Physical Reality (but not the Umbra) exists to hold humans. This is why you can use <s>Spirit</s> DimSci to Format Space redefining reality to what VE think it's &quot;normal&quot;, you're just applying this fundamental principle to make the universe take the form that it naturally should take to hold humans.<br /> <br /> Oh, and only VE pray by this principle to explain gods and ghosts, and other things that should not be. No other convention does. NWO &quot;Information makes Reality&quot; has little to do with the Anthropic Principle.<br /> <br /> B: Only the High Ups of the Technocracy trully know <i>and understand</i> that &quot;What is believed is reality&quot;. The grunts merely apply this enlightened policy (I imagine the White Tower HAS to know this on an intelectual level, but others just believe Deviance it's something that science will explain eventually). Just like most Traditionalists don't really buy the Purple Paradigm. Read the &quot;methaphysics of magic&quot; sidebar again.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Psionics isn't &quot;casting without a focus&quot;. It's casting without a <i>physical </i>focus. And you need to have declared Psionics as a focus you can use (as in, not all technocrats know how to do this nor have the special training or implants), it requires you to have special implements or spend Willpower. You can't just &quot;use it&quot; any more than a Hermetic can use magical kung fu (that is, you can, but you need to have made the effort to add this into your character's foci).<br /> <br /> You seem to confuse the general Paradigm of the Technocracy with the particular Foci that a single Technocrat can use. M20 clears this with it's definitions of Paradigm/Practice/Instruments: You Technocrat may believe in Reason, but he has a way he Practices reason that limits the Instruments of chosing. Instruments themselves need to be learned. There's a reason why ItX agents and VE are much more inclined to use gadgets than NWO, it's because their Practice it's that of Hypertechnology. Any mage can have more than one Practice, and thus your ItX can <i>learn </i>NWO techniques to use sunglasses, but he has to <i>learn </i>them. Otherwise you're casting outside your confort zone-this is possible (any mage can do it) but has a ton of penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-21-2017, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T10:02:24-07:00","id":1142577,"title":"","content":"Psionic spheres. Look them up in guide to the Technocracy. They allow a Technocrat to use spheres with nothing more than the power of will, at chargen.<br /> <br /> What does that sound like to you? To me it sounds like the thing that takes traditional mages getting to Arete 6+ to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T10:45:18-07:00","id":1142591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1142534#post1142534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B: Only the High Ups of the Technocracy trully know <i>and understand</i> that &quot;What is believed is reality&quot;. The grunts merely apply this enlightened policy (I imagine the White Tower HAS to know this on an intelectual level, but others just believe Deviance it's something that science will explain eventually). Just like most Traditionalists don't really buy the Purple Paradigm. Read the &quot;methaphysics of magic&quot; sidebar again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> Remember, everyone, that back in the Renaissance, the Order of Reason divided itself into Outer and Inner Labyrinths. It was a secret, initiatory society, so parts of its knowledge base was withheld from members until they achieved higher ranks, like all secret societies that are built around initiation. The Outer Labyrinth - made up of the unEnlightened Brethren and those Enlightened members of Arete 3 and lower - were deliberately made unaware that what they were doing was anything supernatural, superhuman, or super-scientific. To the point where Mage: The Sorcerer's Crusade recommended the Casual Rule for all such Order of Reason members in the Outer Labyrinth. Which says &quot;you cannot use any Enlightened Effects that are Vain, Period&quot;. They did not believe it was possible, because all Outer Labyrinth members believed they were using techniques available to all humans (with the proper training), or tools and technologies that were reasonable extrapolations of existing ones. To members of the Outer Labyrinth, there was no visible difference between an unEnlightened and Enlightened member, save that the latter may be more skilled, better trained, more knowledgeable of natural philosophy, or simply more lucky/observant/blessed by God's/The Devil's own luck.<br /> <br /> It is only when a Daedalean reaches Arete 4 are they initiated into the Inner Labyrinth, and revealed the truth. That certain people have an ephemeral but rational power of Enlightenment, that pushes them to the peak of human potential. And that this allows rational, God-fearing individuals to push the boundaries of invention, organization, and technique, in order to better mankind's lot in life. And now that the Daedalean has reached the Inner Labyrinth, they are allowed to pursue these more...experimental disciplines and sciences. So long, of course, as the character does not fall to the ever-present temptation of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Naturally, the highest ranking members of the Inner Labyrinth dabble in Sorcery often - or Sorcery-like bits of questionable Science - in secret. But that's neither here nor there. For the Order of Reason, everything is explicable, or will be rendered explicable with time and the proper testing.<br /> <br /> I see no reason to think that the modern Technocracy wouldn't follow the same general arrangement. The rank-and-file in the Union understand only the party line: what they do is nothing more than bleeding edge research, based on the most theoretical and advanced of scientific principles. All of which, naturally, is too advanced to let the general public know about, until such time as the science has been refined. Given that an Enlightened agent doesn't have access to Effects much more powerful than an experienced Extraordinary Citizen (with their focused but not insignificant technosorcery Paths), agents on the ground would be hard pressed to even effectively tell if &quot;Enlightenment&quot; were anything more than a loose identifier for talent.<br /> <br /> And the superstitionists? Why, they are either frauds that cloak legitimate technology behind veneers of mysticism, or idiot savants who stumble into real scientific power, or the blind adherents to ancient proto-science that have nuggets of truth buried in heaps of nonsense, or individuals sensitive to other dimensional beings and capable of inducing such alien organisms to perform for them (likely at terrible cost in the future), or even those who wield dangerous psionic power, barely shackled and directed by ritual and primitive taboos. The fact that the superstitionist is unwilling to perform their most impressive feats outside of situations they rigidly control is evidence that they are charlatans who need to arrange their tricks in advance. That they seem to suffer bizarre backlashes from their efforts at times speaks of not being in true control of the forces they channel. That the ones who claim to speak to &quot;spirits&quot; adhere to insane behavioral patterns is evidence that they are either being forced to comply with requests from truly alien intelligences, or they are psionics who suffer from schizophrenia and hallucinations.<br /> <br /> It is only when a Technocrat rises to the highest ranks that they are informed of the truth: that Reality, to some degree, responds to human belief. Which is exactly why the Union's mission of educating the masses in one world view is so vital. Of course, anyone who reaches that level has been allowed to advance because they've proven discreet, trustworthy, and loyal to the Union and its principles. That way, even as their old beliefs are revealed as half-truth, they are already committed to the Technocracy, and can see the brutal necessity of the deception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T11:35:04-07:00","id":1142622,"title":"","content":"Well, let's not get crazy. I may be unwiling to believe without quotes from the book that all Technocrats can just use their &quot;psychic powers&quot; to avoid focus , or that they don't have to chose foci/instruments. But lets them go Vulgar at least, so they can use their plasma canons (or the &quot;special&quot; guns that were Vulgar in cruzade) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T12:49:51-07:00","id":1142659,"title":"","content":"The issue with that is that the modern technocracy pretty much throws that out the window. Every 'recruitment' scene I've read in the books has involved outright TELLING the recruit that magic is real and needs policing. Aside from the brainwashing scenes of course. If you're enlightened, you're in on the joke. Now, there are Proles/Kamrads/Etc who aren't in on it. But that's a different matter entirely. If you're Enlightened, you know.<br /> <br /> And no, they can't just use psychic powers. They have to declare up to two spheres psionic spheres during chargen. Or to quote the book.<br /> <br /> &quot;We recommend that no agent be allowed to have more<br /> than two Spheres declared as \u201cpsionic\u201d Spheres. These Spheres<br /> can be used with just a turn of concentration and maybe<br /> a gesture or a withering stare. On the downside, Paradox<br /> manifestations tend to backlash in nasty neurological fashion;<br /> the Progenitors have a lab wing full of comatose, vegetative<br /> drooling subjects who overreached their psionic limits. Psionics<br /> is a barely understood or accepted science even within<br /> the Union, and its use will be monitored.&quot; ~ Guide to the Technocracy, Page 48.<br /> <br /> Obviously, such effects are as vulgar as any traditional fireball, but they can be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T13:17:53-07:00","id":1142671,"title":"","content":"Think there were additional rules on how exactly to handle psychic paradigms somewhere. May even have been M20 or HDYDT (though I don't really like what they did in that book). Psychic paradigms usually are not just &quot;I can just do this lol&quot;. They often require intense concentration (spending wp or taking more time) or extensive biological modification or implants (and the resultant maintenance can be a nightmare, see the example in the revised progenitor convention book)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T14:37:24-07:00","id":1142700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1142671#post1142671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think there were additional rules on how exactly to handle psychic paradigms somewhere. May even have been M20 or HDYDT (though I don't really like what they did in that book). Psychic paradigms usually are not just &amp;quot;I can just do this lol&amp;quot;. They often require intense concentration (spending wp or taking more time) or extensive biological modification or implants (and the resultant maintenance can be a nightmare, see the example in the revised progenitor convention book)</div> </div> </div> </div>In M20? Yes. But M20's take on magic is so ridiculously baroque and overworked as to be idiotic. As demonstrated by their take on basically everything.<br /> <br /> In revised, that was the extent of the rules for psychic spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T15:22:29-07:00","id":1142719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1142700#post1142700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In M20? Yes. But M20's take on magic is so ridiculously baroque and overworked as to be idiotic. As demonstrated by their take on basically everything.<br /> <br /> In revised, that was the extent of the rules for psychic spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with HDYDT overdoing it to the point of ridiculously, this version of a psychic paradigm is just as bad, really. Paradigm allways should involve fluff, &quot;I just do it&quot; has no fluff to it. And to be honest Guide to the Technocracy wasn't exactly good when it came to portraying technocratic magic. It was an interesting and necessary step in the evolution of the TU from 2 dimensional bad guys to the grey idealistic yet corrupt organization that we saw in the revised convention books (and sadly it seemed to me M20 was taking a step back again... but I guess my issues with M20 are not the point here). But its magic section was just not using the technocratic paradigm at all in some parts. I remember a rote where a technocrat was supposed to whirl around, teleporting a weapon into his hand aswell. Why? Because it was totally coincidental because he could have had a weapon. Yeah right that's great, but that's not using the paradigm of the TU at all. The TU does not just willwork. Their methods may seem identical at face level, but ultimatly the TU believes in rules. They believe their magic allows them work within and even change the rules of the universe.. But they don't do so by just wishing it strongly, they do it through precise manipulation of the laws as they exist. I personally wouldn't enforce spending wp for psychic magic, but a technocrat who uses psychic abilities to work his magic allmost certainly has a structured and well documented (among the union) approach to this, likely involving some alteration of his pattern to enable the use of such abilities. They don't just willwork, that is superstitionist talk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T15:23:58-07:00","id":1142721,"title":"","content":"Taken from M20 in the SCIENCE!!! on page 290<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;The flip side to this technomagickal advantage is that science-based reality-alteration doesn\u2019t just have to be accepted by a bunch of stupid Sleepers: the technomancer must believe in it as well. Sure, his theories might be skewed, demented, even impossible by normal scientific standards, but they must make sense\u2026 at least to him, and probably to the people he respects. A Progenitor hypergeneticist, for example, might be able to clone a werewolf, isolate \u201cthe changing gene,\u201d or kill the beast with an infusion of silver nitrate. He could not, however, simply wave his hand and turn the werewolf to silver. That\u2019s not science! Awakened/ Inspired Science can get pretty weird, but \u2013 according to the beliefs of the people who use it \u2013 it cannot do the impossible.<br /> <br /> Thus, technomagick is a double-edged scalpel: you can use it more freely in the modern world, but it must make a certain degree of sense within a scientific belief system. If it does not, the character himself does not believe in the results\u2026 and we all know what happens when Wile E. Coyote looks down and sees that he\u2019s running on thin air. In game terms, a Storyteller may feel free to call shenanigans on a player\u2019s explanation when that explanation does not fit the character\u2019s belief system. </b><br /> <br /> <i><b>If the Progenitor mentioned above tried to explain his silvery wave as \u201cdisrupting the molecular structure and shifting the elemental spectrum through my new theory of manual destabilizing conversion,\u201d then POOF! It\u2019s vulgar magick. No scientific coincidences for you! This offers clever challenges for the technomantic player, provides fun roleplaying material, and forces him to think of his deeds in terms of the character\u2019s beliefs. &quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> According to passages like this, if it fits in your paradigm you can justify it with advanced science. A theory still technically counts as a focus I suppose, but for something like the example that sounds vulgar as hell and I bet most ST's woulden't let it past. I always liked the idea that mages can do <b>'ANYTHING', </b>but in reality it seems kind of crazy to allow hand waving and a theory for a full size transformation. <br /> <br /> Then again, in Futurama bender can go back in time by reciting binary code.....so whatever. Maybe once arete get high enough you can justify internalizing foci at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16848-brassfist","name":"Brassfist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T15:51:35-07:00","id":1142729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brassfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1142721#post1142721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taken from M20 in the SCIENCE!!! on page 290<br /> Maybe once arete get high enough you can justify internalizing foci at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, of course, M20 explicitly states that Technocrats can't do that. Period. Other technomancers might be able to overcome their Instruments, but Technocrats can't. Not just because of their Paradigm, but because of the Conditioning that all operatives undergo when they join the Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T18:17:50-07:00","id":1142770,"title":"","content":"Relevant to the discussion on Psionics: this practice is covered in M20 Book of Secrets on page 203 in great detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T20:05:30-07:00","id":1142797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1142729#post1142729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, of course, M20 explicitly states that Technocrats can't do that. Period. Other technomancers might be able to overcome their Instruments, but Technocrats can't. Not just because of their Paradigm, but because of the Conditioning that all operatives undergo when they join the Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I say internalize, I don't mean losing it via purple paradigm I mean changing focus to a internalized one. I probably should have clarified that I didn't mean dropping the focus, as technocrats never do that as far as I can remember. The idea that a technocrat has such a good understanding of physics that he knows the right thought form that can induce tears in spacetime or shoot microwaves from his hands with the mathematical calculation of how. Much like a virtual adept &quot;doing the math&quot; to hack reality, my thought was that at higher arete it would be easier for technocrats to do this hyperscience like what the quote says, turning a werewolf to silver without a device, albeit with huge risk of paradox of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16848-brassfist","name":"Brassfist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T08:36:59-07:00","id":1142918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea that a technocrat has such a good understanding of physics that he knows the right thought form that can induce tears in spacetime or shoot microwaves from his hands with the mathematical calculation of how. Much like a virtual adept &quot;doing the math&quot; to hack reality </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but you still need to make the calculations (possibly making a Science or Esoterics check), much like your psion needs to have the &quot;special implants/biomods/CIA psionic training/whatever&quot; to use his psionics, (and that's why a Technocrat can't just &quot;do it&quot; if he forgot his techno-gun). Anyone can use Skills as a focus. A NWO agent could be teached a dangerous meme that must only be disclosed under extreme caution because it melts the eyes of the observer. NWO has code words that when uttered activate hidden hypnotic comands that were implanted into the populace trough media control, like the Illuminatus that they are. Some may say this looks a lot like a magick word, but this isn't &quot;casting without an instrument&quot; any more than a Hermetic using enochian or an Akashick using meditation, or a Etherite using psionics. It all makes sense under Paradigm, and you need to be trained in the use of these tools if you don't want to suffer penalties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> my thought was that at higher arete it would be easier for technocrats to do this hyperscience like what the quote says, turning a werewolf to silver without a device, albeit with huge risk of paradox of course. </div> </div> </div>I do think this would be a good hack. It would represent mechanically the secrets that supposedly only the &quot;high ups&quot; understand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with that is that the modern technocracy pretty much throws that out the window. Every 'recruitment' scene I've read in the books has involved outright TELLING the recruit that magic is real and needs policing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Telling that magic it's real it's not the same as telling you that you're going to do magic under the guise of science. Knowing that reality it's (more or less) Consensual isn't the same as thinking that the &quot;advanced&quot; principles you use only work because you're willing them too work, Technocracy believes that the opinion of the masses it's important, but they don't put a lot of weight in the opinions of the individual, that's why they don't do &quot;willworking&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T21:54:21-07:00","id":1143970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1142659#post1142659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with that is that the modern technocracy pretty much throws that out the window. Every 'recruitment' scene I've read in the books has involved outright TELLING the recruit that magic is real and needs policing. Aside from the brainwashing scenes of course. If you're enlightened, you're in on the joke. Now, there are Proles/Kamrads/Etc who aren't in on it. But that's a different matter entirely. If you're Enlightened, you know.<br /> <br /> And no, they can't just use psychic powers. They have to declare up to two spheres psionic spheres during chargen. Or to quote the book.<br /> <br /> &quot;We recommend that no agent be allowed to have more<br /> than two Spheres declared as \u201cpsionic\u201d Spheres. These Spheres<br /> can be used with just a turn of concentration and maybe<br /> a gesture or a withering stare. On the downside, Paradox<br /> manifestations tend to backlash in nasty neurological fashion;<br /> the Progenitors have a lab wing full of comatose, vegetative<br /> drooling subjects who overreached their psionic limits. Psionics<br /> is a barely understood or accepted science even within<br /> the Union, and its use will be monitored.&quot; ~ Guide to the Technocracy, Page 48.<br /> <br /> Obviously, such effects are as vulgar as any traditional fireball, but they can be done.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A psychic focus is still a psychic focus. Its like saying meditation isn't a focus because it just looks like he sits there and shit happens. The Technocrat spends a turn or more concentrating and shit happens. That's not &quot;free surpassed focus&quot; a Mage who has surpassed focus would just act without having to do that turn of setup.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T07:46:44-07:00","id":1144063,"title":"","content":"Unless the Operative has Procedures which revolve around being unarmed (Krav Maga, which is quote scientific, or stuff like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marine_Corps_Martial_Arts_Program)\" target=\"_blank\">the Marine Martial Arts program</a> , then they are literally SOL, much like a Superstitionist without tools is. As of Revised, all Mages need tools. Also, all Technocrats are *fully* aware that what they do is changing subjective reality - they just do it in the sanest, best and most rational system possible, because Sleepers can not be trusted with power. The NWO book makes this absolutely clear. This non-canonical notion that Technocrats don't know that they are changing subjective reality via will is something which left the line as of 2nd Edition. Any Enlightened Operative is fully aware that Reality is subjective and that it must be kept in it's current form for Sleeper society not to descend into madness. The Union paradigm is modern day capitalism and liberal economics on a magickal scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T16:37:58-07:00","id":1144226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1143970#post1143970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A psychic focus is still a psychic focus. Its like saying meditation isn't a focus because it just looks like he sits there and shit happens. The Technocrat spends a turn or more concentrating and shit happens. That's not &quot;free surpassed focus&quot; a Mage who has surpassed focus would just act without having to do that turn of setup.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the Technocrat simply does a thing. There's no 'turn of set up' they spend their turn doing magic/psychic nonsense. Surpassing your foci doesn't give you an extra action to do magic with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T12:48:34-07:00","id":1144516,"title":"","content":"&quot;A turn of <b>concentration</b>...doing magic/psychic nonsense&quot; implies a mental effort that may prevent doing other things or call for penalties. Also, there are rotes that require &quot;concentration&quot; to mantain, and RAW you can't do activities that require concentration where you're keeping them. A meditation or similar roll could be called if it's a distressing situation where concentrating isn't easy. Someone could try to break your &quot;concentration&quot;....evil ST can do wonders with those three words. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Surpassing your foci doesn't give you an extra action to do magic with. </div> </div> </div>It does allow you to do other stuff while you're casting. Talking being the primary example. <br /> <br /> Usually people do not want to be in a conversation while they're really concentrating on something, to the point that &quot;shut up, I'm trying to concentrate&quot; it's a common (if rude) expresion. <hr />Also: &quot;<i>Psionics </i><i>is a barely understood or accepted </i>science even within the Union, and its use will be monitored.&quot; Psionics isn't a very good example of how Technocrats work, as they barely accept or understand it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T13:34:15-07:00","id":1144528,"title":"","content":"Oh it's not standard at all. The point is less &quot;Any technocrat is gonna just bust out their psychic powers if you catch them naked and unarmed!&quot; and more emphasizing that the Technocratic Paradigm is more or less a Systematic exploitation of the Purple Paradigm for perceived tactical, strategic, and logistical advantage to serve their goal of creating a world of Objective laws out of the world of subjective laws they live in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T21:07:48-07:00","id":1144625,"title":"","content":"Minor nitpick: Technocrats do not all share a singular Paradigm. If they did, there wouldn't be separate Conventions and Divisions within those Conventions. They are unified in their overall goals and ideals but they are almost as diverse as the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T06:51:52-07:00","id":1144743,"title":"","content":"Of course, the difference being that each of the conventions have a schtick. And inside that schtick the others acknowledge their paradigm as law. Each convention might have their own pet projects using those spheres. But by and large you would learn Mind from the NWO. Matter or Forces from Iteration X's, Life from the progenitors, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T13:03:47-07:00","id":1144906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1144743#post1144743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the difference being that each of the conventions have a schtick. And inside that schtick the others acknowledge their paradigm as law. Each convention might have their own pet projects using those spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But by and large you would learn Mind from the NWO. Matter or Forces from Iteration X's, Life from the progenitors, etc. </div> </div> </div>But not quite with this. While cross teaching it's used among the Technocracy, each Convention has it's own ways to use all the Spheres, and that's the approach that they learn most of the time. A typical ItX member will learn Mind to create a better AI, perfect her brain implants or nanobots, create gadgets that read and manipulate the mind. She ain't going to be learning MiB detectivesque approach to read someones mind, but merely learn how to hack a brain from her computer, something that can be done with ItX approach to Mind and thus doesn't need to be outsourced.<br /> <br /> I think you're confusing things. Technocrats work together a lot. If you need to program a human like AI, you may call the NWO for agents that know Mind and they will help with their expertice in &quot;human behavior&quot;, but that doesn't mean that NWO are the only dudes that can teach you Mind, nor the ones that will teach you how to *program* an AI (they're merely consultants that give you a bonus)<br /> <br /> Technocrats accept that all conventions use valid methods, but usually keep with their own methods (because they're obviously better than those of the other Conventions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T17:05:20-07:00","id":1145390,"title":"","content":"Yes. The different Conventions all have their own processes for the different Spheres (Sciences?). With Mind, the Progenitors are probably the ones trying to breed working psychic abilities as part of their plans to create a master race ruling over a world that looks like Brave New World or SM Stirling's Draka books, while the NWO are more focused on methods of intimidation via authority, brainwashing, re-education facilitates, and memory holes as part of the Orwellian goal of ultimately getting everyone to think exactly alike and obey authority, and the Void Engineers are more interested in defending against and purging extra-human influences from their own operatives and humanity in general (with psychonauts delving into the depths of the human mind as a means to this end), Iteration X trying to perfect human thought processes via training, cybernetic implants and teaching software as part of building better cogs for the machine, and the Syndicate focused on the applied psychological warfare that is advertising, memes and salesmanship as part of convincing the masses that the elite are better than you and you want to do whatever it takes to curry their favor and try to join them. <br /> <br /> I really wish more had been done in Mage with the concept of Memory Palaces and other mnemonics. They are pretty fascinating tools and you can see them in some of Thomas Harris's Hannibal Lector novels and Stephen King's Dreamcatcher, among other places. They fit very well with Technocratic Mind science, as well as that of the Hermetics, Virtual Adepts and Etherites. Probably Batini, Lions of Zion, Akashics and Thanatoics as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T19:09:48-07:00","id":1145419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140399-what-can-an-unarmed-technocrat-do?p=1145390#post1145390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really wish more had been done in Mage with the concept of Memory Palaces and other mnemonics. They are pretty fascinating tools and you can see them in some of Thomas Harris's Hannibal Lector novels and Stephen King's Dreamcatcher, among other places. They fit very well with Technocratic Mind science, as well as that of the Hermetics, Virtual Adepts and Etherites. Probably Batini, Lions of Zion, Akashics and Thanatoics as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, although we can work out some of the basics with what we have. A Memory Palace could count as a Thought Form of sorts, in terms of Instruments. (Or Meditation, whichever). By walking one's personal Palace, Temple, Mindscape, or Labyrinth, the mage can perform various feats. Like a Batini who establishes a shield against mental assault by getting lost in her labyrinth. Or a Hermetic who performs a High Ritual entirely in his personal mental temple, imagining in great detail every prop, set dressing, and ritual assistant (just read Self-Initiation Into The Golden Dawn Tradition, and how a person without an entire order of other people has to perform their initiation rite while imagining various figures that take the place of other Golden Dawn members). Or a Virtual Adept &quot;programming&quot; a virtual space in their heads, and using it to access the web through the great electromagnetic network across the planet (see also Serial Experiments Lain). Or any mage imagining a door at the border of their Palace, and using a physical object of someone's as a &quot;key&quot;, letting the mage open the door and enter the person's mind.<br /> <br /> A character with a Memory Palace might also benefit from the Demesne background, to establish that their particular mental space is so well established, it has a presence in the land of dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 09-29-2017, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}